Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, podman (>= 4.9), systemd, polkitd, procps, openssh-client, libcurl4t64, libcurl3t64-gnutls, libqt6sql6-sqlite, qt6-qpa-plugins, qt6-wayland, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-window, qml6-module-qtqml, qml6-module-qtqml-models, qml6-module-qtqml-workerscript, qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs, qml6-module-qt5compat-graphicaleffects
Recommends: qemu-kvm, qemu-utils, virtiofsd, caddy, docker-compose-v2 | docker-compose, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: Native desktop for Podman containers, VMs and Kubernetes
 PodStack provides containers, images, volumes, networks, Compose projects,
 QEMU/KVM machines, Kubernetes and local HTTPS domains in one native Linux
 application. The GUI and CLI talk to a per-user daemon over a 0600 Unix
 socket; privileged setup actions use an allowlisted polkit helper.
